### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a rectangular block with some content) that flips/rotates when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;          /* width of the card */
  height: 200px;         /* height of the card */
  perspective: 1000px;   /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;     /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card (the element that rotates) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card .face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #fff;
  border-radius: 10px;
}

.card .front {
  background: #3498db;   /* front face colour */
}

.card .back {
  background: #e74c3c;   /* back face colour */
  transform: rotateY(180deg); /* start rotated so it's hidden */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg); /* flip the card on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="face front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="face back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper creates a 3‑D space. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3‑D. |
| **3** | Two faces (`front` and `back`) are absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the back side when it’s turned away. |
| **4** | On hover, the whole card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

#### Customisation tips

- Change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip.
- Adjust `perspective` value for stronger/weaker depth.
- Replace colours, fonts, or add images inside the faces.
- Add more complex transitions (e.g., `transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(...)`) for different easing.

Enjoy experimenting!
